# Git push with GITHUB_TOKEN

When the user asks to push commits to GitHub:

1. Load `GITHUB_TOKEN` from the repo-root `.env` (never print, log, or commit it).
2. Push over HTTPS as `https://x-access-token:${GITHUB_TOKEN}@github.com/<owner>/<repo>.git` for the current branch.
3. Do not depend on interactive `gh` or Windows credential-manager prompts.
4. Never stage or commit `.env`.
5. Verify with `git status -sb` after push.

If the token is missing or rejected, ask the user to update `.env` — do not invent credentials.

See also: [cursor-rules.md](../../cursor-rules.md)
